Stop the olr service and remove it from boot.

The unit files stay where they are, so `olr enable` brings it back
without reinstalling anything. Configuration and state are untouched.

Backends keep serving: stopping the control plane never interrupts
DHCP or DNS. Use `olr dhcp disable` and `olr dns disable` for those.

Usage:
  olr disable [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for disable

Global Flags:
      --dry-run         show what would change and exit without applying it
  -o, --output string   output format: text|json (default "text")
      --socket string   olrd control socket (default "/run/olr/olrd.sock")
